BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//OmniSource//Release calendar//EN
CALSCALE:GREGORIAN
X-WR-CALNAME:UTM releases
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:utm-5.0.8@omnisource
DTSTAMP:20261017T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:UTM v5.0.8
DESCRIPTION:UTM 5.0.8 | Universal IPA\n\n## Highlights\n* (macOS) **DirectX
  graphics support for Windows**: Modern accelerated graphics for Windows 1
 1 is now available on UTM for the first time. The driver is still experime
 ntal and games compatibility is currently limited.\n* **Vulkan 1.3 graphic
 s support for Linux**: Vulkan 1.3 is now supported on Linux guests with Vi
 rtIO Venus drivers in Mesa. Additionally\, OpenGL 4.1 is supported with th
 e new Apple Core OpenGL backend (macOS only).\n* **Snapshots**: Save your 
 VM at any point and go back to it later from the new Snapshots tab. Works 
 with QEMU VMs on macOS and iOS 26\, and with Apple Virtualization VMs on m
 acOS 27.\n* (macOS) **Apple Virtualization on macOS 27**: Pass USB devices
  through to your VM\, turn on Secure Boot for Linux\, run a VM without sav
 ing changes\, and let VMs talk to each other with new networking modes.\n*
  (iOS) **Better touch controls**: Gestures respond immediately\, with new 
 middle-click and right-drag actions and a new drag-to-scroll touch mode.\n
 * (iOS) **iPhone Duo**: Fold your iPhone Duo like a laptop\, and the botto
 m half becomes a keyboard or touchpad for your VM.\n\n## Notes\n* Suspende
 d VMs may not resume correctly after updating. We recommend shutting down 
 all VMs before you update UTM.\n* The minimum supported versions are now m
 acOS 12 and iOS 15.\n* We now have a [development blog](https://blog.getut
 m.app)! Follow us for in-depth technical deep dives such as how we brought
  DirectX to QEMU.\n* (macOS) To use the new graphics driver for Windows 11
 \, we recommend a fresh install because the driver is still experimental a
 nd its use could lead to instability in the system. During the install of 
 the guest tools\, you will be prompted to select the experimental graphics
  driver. If you wish to install the new driver on a system that already is
  running the older display only driver\, you need to run the uninstall scr
 ipt provided on the guest tools install ISO first.\n* (macOS) Apple CoreGL
  backend does not support Vulkan or Di
URL:https://raynmahbub.github.io/OmniSource/feeds/utm.json
END:VEVENT
